  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S. Murari Lal Harish Chandra Jaiswal ... vs The Commissioner Of Food Safety on 5 August, 2024 Author: M.Dhandapani Bench: M.Dhandapani WP.No.28266 of In the High Court of Judicature at Madras Dated : 05.08.2024 Coram : The Honourable Mr.Justice M.Dhandapani Writ Petition No.28266 of 2021 M/s. Murari Lal Harish Chandra Jaiswal Pvt. Ltd., Represented by its Authorized Signatory, Mr.K.Prabhakaran, 6043, Naya Bans, Delhi 110 006. ... Pe Vs 1. The Commissioner of Food Safety, 5th Floor, Dms Office Building, 359, Anna Salai, Dms Campus, Teynampet, Chennai 600 006. 2. The Designated Officer, Tamil Nadu Food Safety & Drug, Administration Department, Food Safety Wing, 54/1, Asoori Street, Tiruvallur District. ...Respo Petition under Article 226 of The Constitution of India prayin the issuance of a Writ of Certiorarified Mandamus to call for the record the file of the 2nd respondent in his proceedings vide Lr.Ref.No.274/A1/ dated 16.11.2021 and quash the same and subsequently direct the respondents and their men from anyway taking any punitive action in respect of the petitioner's product namely, Hans Chaap Tobacco in view https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 1/8 WP.No.28266 M/S. Murari Lal Harish Chandra Jaiswal ... vs The Commissioner Of Food Safety on 5 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/102033457/ 1 of the final orders dated 02.12.2016, 06.03.2017, 07.09.2017, 05.11.2020 and 04.12.2020 passed in respect of the above product by the Referral Fo Laboratories situated in Pune and Mysore respectively. For Petitioner : Mr.L.Goutham Raj For Respondents : Mr.P.Kumaresan, Aag Assisted by Mr.E.Sundaram, Ga Order",
    "facts": "2. The petitioner is a registered unit, carrying on the business of trading of tobacco, namely HANS Chaap Tobacco, after getting all statutory approvals and by paying requisite taxes. According to the petitioners, HANS Chaap Tobacco would not come under the category of food or pan https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis masala and the respondents have no authority to interfere with the business of the petitioners. 3. While so, the Food Safety Officer, during his official duty, seized from a retailer, the product namely, HANS Chaap Tobacco under the provisions of the FSSAI Act and sent the sample for the Food Analyst, Food Analysis Laboratory at King Institute Campus, Guindy, Chennai in terms of Section 38(1)(a)(b) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. Thereafter, the 2nd respondent served the report of the Food Analyst, dated 24.09.2021 along with proceedings of the second respondent dated 30.09.2021 on the petitioner stating that the sample found is banned food product-tobacco falling under Regulation 2.12 of Food Safety and Standards (Food Products Standards and Food Additives) Regulations, 2011. Aggrieved by the Food Analyst Report, dated 24.09.2021 and the proceedings of the 2nd respondent dated 30.09.2021, the petitioner preferred appeal before the 2nd respondent. However, the 2nd respondent vide order dated 16.11.2021, rejected the appeal.",
    "arguments": "4. When this Writ Petition is taken up for hearing, the learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that admittedly, the 2 nd respondent has passed the impugned order without affording an opportunity of hearing to the petitioner and without sending the sample for re-analysis to the Food Analyst which is per se unsustainable. He further submits that this Court, vide order dated 07.03.2024 in W.P.Nos.4457 of 2022 etc., after taking note of the fact that the impugned orders have been passed contrary to the principles of natural justice, while setting aside the impugned M/S. Murari Lal Harish Chandra Jaiswal ... vs The Commissioner Of Food Safety on 5 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/102033457/ 2 orders on the ground of principles of natural justice, directed for re-hearing of the appeals and to pass orders de novo in accordance with law. Therefore, the learned counsel would urge this Court to pass similar order in the present Writ Petition also."
  },
